// 초고가 나온 뒤 실린 문장에서 추출한다. kind=web 은 웹 원문의 서술이나 수치, derived 는 이 문서가 원문 차트 점으로 계산한 값. evidence 는 evidence.jsonl 의 span 을 그대로 옮겼다.
{"id":"c1","kind":"web","text":"소개 글이 코드 변경으로 적은 것은 thinking 을 끄던 사람은 between_tools 로 바꾸라는 한 문장이다 (01, 17장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w1 §Getting started","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Getting started","quote":"If you run Sonnet with thinking off, you’ll need to switch to the new between_tools setting, which keeps up-front thinking off, before moving to Sonnet 5.5."}]}
{"id":"c2","kind":"web","text":"가격은 Sonnet 5 와 같아 입력 $2, 출력 $10, 캐시 읽기 $0.20 이고 원문은 태스크당 최대 30% 싸다고 쓴다 (02, 10장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w1 §intro · Cost, d1 §intro","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§intro · Cost","quote":"Sonnet 5.5 is priced the same as Sonnet 5 at $2 per million input tokens, $10 per million output tokens, and $0.20 per million tokens for cache reads, but it typically needs far fewer tokens to do the same work. In our testing, it costs up to 30% less per task than its predecessor."},{"source":"d1","locator":"§intro ¶2","quote":"Claude Sonnet 5.5 has the same prices as Claude Sonnet 5."}]}
{"id":"c3","kind":"web","text":"between_tools 는 low, medium, high 에서만 받고 xhigh 와 max 에서는 400 이다 (02, 04, 14, 18장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d1 §Turn off up-front thinking","evidence":[{"source":"d1","locator":"§Turn off up-front thinking ¶2","quote":"`between_tools` works on every platform that offers Claude Sonnet 5.5, with no beta header. It's accepted at `low`, `medium`, and `high` effort. At `xhigh` or `max`, it returns a 400 error."}]}
{"id":"c4","kind":"web","text":"Sonnet 5.5 에서 thinking disabled 는 400 이고 허용 값은 adaptive 와 between_tools 이며 Sonnet 5 는 disabled 를 받았다 (04장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d1 §Thinking runs by default, §Turn off up-front thinking","evidence":[{"source":"d1","locator":"§Thinking runs by default · table","quote":"| Claude Sonnet 5.5                      | On                                  | `\"adaptive\"`, `\"between_tools\"`                      | `\"omitted\"`       |"},{"source":"d1","locator":"§Thinking runs by default · table","quote":"| Claude Sonnet 5                        | On                                  | `\"adaptive\"`, `\"disabled\"`                           | `\"omitted\"`       |"},{"source":"d1","locator":"§Turn off up-front thinking ¶1","quote":"On Claude Sonnet 5.5, `disabled` returns a 400 `invalid_request_error`:"}]}
{"id":"c5","kind":"web","text":"between_tools 는 답하기 전 thinking 을 끄고 tool call 사이 진행 메모만 thinking 블록으로 남기며 도구가 없으면 텍스트뿐이다 (04장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d1 §Turn off up-front thinking","evidence":[{"source":"d1","locator":"§Turn off up-front thinking ¶1","quote":"To turn off up-front thinking on Claude Sonnet 5.5, send `thinking: {\"type\": \"between_tools\"}`. It's the lowest thinking setting. Its progress updates between tool calls still come back as `thinking` blocks with their summary text. Without tools, the response contains only text."}]}
{"id":"c6","kind":"web","text":"between_tools 에 display, budget_tokens, block_binding 을 함께 보내면 400 이고 fallback 으로 Sonnet 5 에 가면 disabled 로 돈다 (04장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d1 §Turn off up-front thinking","evidence":[{"source":"d1","locator":"§Turn off up-front thinking ¶2","quote":"`between_tools` takes no other field: `display`, `budget_tokens`, or `block_binding` sent with it returns a 400 error. With [server-side fallback](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/refusals-and-fallback#server-side-fallback), a `between_tools` request that falls back to Claude Sonnet 5 runs there with `thinking: {\"type\": \"disabled\"}`."}]}
{"id":"c7","kind":"web","text":"between_tools 에서는 대화 중 메시지별 effort 를 다르게 보내면 400 이다 (04, 14장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d1 §Turn off up-front thinking","evidence":[{"source":"d1","locator":"§Turn off up-front thinking ¶3","quote":"With `between_tools`, effort can't change mid-conversation: a per-message `output_config.effort` that differs from the level in effect returns a 400 error."}]}
{"id":"c8","kind":"web","text":"tool_choice 의 any 와 tool 은 token counting 을 포함해 400 이고 대체는 auto 와 strict: true 다 (05장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d1 §Forced tool use","evidence":[{"source":"d1","locator":"§Forced tool use","quote":"Every earlier model on this page accepts a `tool_choice` of type `any` or `tool`. Claude Sonnet 5.5 rejects both with a 400 error, including on the [token counting](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/token-counting) endpoint:"},{"source":"d1","locator":"§Forced tool use ¶2","quote":"Send `tool_choice: {\"type\": \"auto\"}`, and mark the tool `strict: true` so its input matches the schema. The model can then answer without calling the tool, so say in the prompt when to use it."}]}
{"id":"c9","kind":"web","text":"Bedrock 에서는 strict tool use 를 포함한 structured outputs 를 Sonnet 5.5 에 쓸 수 없어 auto 만 보내고 입력은 코드에서 검증한다 (05, 14장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d1 §Forced tool use","evidence":[{"source":"d1","locator":"§Forced tool use ¶2","quote":"On Amazon Bedrock, [structured outputs](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/structured-outputs), which include strict tool use, aren't available for Claude Sonnet 5.5. There, send `auto` without `strict`, say in the prompt when to call the tool, and validate the tool input in your code."}]}
{"id":"c10","kind":"web","text":"요청 하나에 strict tool 은 최대 20개이고 MCP, computer use, browser use toolset 은 strict 를 받지 않는다 (05장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d1 §Forced tool use","evidence":[{"source":"d1","locator":"§Forced tool use ¶3","quote":"A request can have at most 20 strict tools, and the MCP, computer use, and browser use toolset entries don't accept `strict`."}]}
{"id":"c11","kind":"web","text":"Claude Managed Agents 는 모델 이름 말고는 바꿀 것이 없다 (05장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d1 §intro note","evidence":[{"source":"d1","locator":"§intro note","quote":"If you use [Claude Managed Agents](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/overview), no changes beyond updating the model name are required."}]}
{"id":"c12","kind":"web","text":"Sonnet 5.5 는 Sonnet 5, Opus 4.8, Haiku 4.5 이전의 블록을 읽고 Opus 5, Opus 5.5, Fable, Mythos 블록은 읽지 못해 버리며 200 을 돌려주고 과금하지 않는다 (06장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d1 §Thinking blocks are tied","evidence":[{"source":"d1","locator":"§Thinking blocks are tied ¶1","quote":"Claude Sonnet 5.5 reads thinking blocks from Claude Sonnet 5, Claude Opus 4.8, Claude Haiku 4.5, and earlier models. It doesn't read blocks from Claude Opus 5, Claude Opus 5.5, or any Claude Fable or Claude Mythos model. The API drops blocks the model can't read. The request still returns 200, and dropped blocks aren't billed."}]}
{"id":"c13","kind":"web","text":"2026-08-31 00:00 UTC 이후 만든 계정은 Claude API, Bedrock, Google Cloud 에서 앞선 대화를 고친 뒤 블록을 다시 보내면 400 이다 (06, 14장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d1 §Thinking blocks are tied","evidence":[{"source":"d1","locator":"§Thinking blocks are tied ¶2","quote":"For accounts created on or after August 31, 2026, 00:00 UTC, the API enforces this by default, on the Claude API, Amazon Bedrock, and Google Cloud. On those accounts, a request that replays a block after an edit to earlier history returns a 400 error."}]}
{"id":"c14","kind":"web","text":"Sonnet 5.5 의 thinking 블록은 만든 계정이나 연결된 계정에서만 쓰인다 (06, 14장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d1 §Thinking blocks are tied","evidence":[{"source":"d1","locator":"§Thinking blocks are tied ¶2","quote":"Thinking blocks that Claude Sonnet 5.5 produces work only in the account that produced them, or in an account linked to it."}]}
{"id":"c15","kind":"web","text":"원문은 Sonnet 최초로 reasoning extraction 분류기를 달고 preserved thinking 을 넓혔으며 대부분의 개발자는 변화를 모를 것이라고 쓴다 (06장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w1 §Safety · Distillation","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Safety · Safeguards · Distillation","quote":"it’s the first Sonnet model to launch with safety classifiers that prevent reasoning extraction. Sonnet 5.5 also expands preserved thinking, so Claude’s thinking cannot be decoupled from the account that created it. Most developers won’t notice a change. If you move conversations between accounts, including switching accounts mid-session in Claude Code, our docs article explains the change."}]}
{"id":"c16","kind":"web","text":"Claude API 와 Google Cloud 에서 computer_20251124 는 400 이고 toolset 만 받으며 computer_20250124 는 모든 플랫폼에서 받지 않는다 (07, 14장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d1 §Computer use","evidence":[{"source":"d1","locator":"§Computer use","quote":"On the Claude API and Google Cloud, Claude Sonnet 5.5 supports computer use only through the `computer_toolset_20260801` toolset. There, `computer_20251124` returns a 400 error. Claude Sonnet 5.5 doesn't accept `computer_20250124` on any platform."}]}
{"id":"c17","kind":"web","text":"fine-grained-tool-streaming beta header 는 toolset 과 함께 보내면 400 이고 eager_input_streaming 으로 대신한다 (07장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d1 §Computer use","evidence":[{"source":"d1","locator":"§Computer use ¶2","quote":"If you send the `fine-grained-tool-streaming-2025-05-14` beta header, remove it when you move to the toolset. Alongside a toolset entry, it returns a 400 error. Set `eager_input_streaming: true` on each tool that needs it instead."}]}
{"id":"c18","kind":"web","text":"Sonnet 5.5 실행자의 advisor 는 Opus 5, Opus 5.5, Sonnet 5.5, Fable 5, Fable 5.1, Mythos 5, Mythos 5.1 이고 Opus 4.6~4.8, Sonnet 5, Sonnet 4.6 은 400 이며 조언은 암호화되어 온다 (07, 14장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d1 §Advisor tool","evidence":[{"source":"d1","locator":"§Advisor tool","quote":"With the [advisor tool](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/advisor-tool), a Claude Sonnet 5.5 executor needs one of these advisors: Claude Opus 5, Claude Opus 5.5, Claude Sonnet 5.5, Claude Fable 5, Claude Fable 5.1, Claude Mythos 5, or Claude Mythos 5.1. Claude Opus 4.8, Claude Opus 4.7, Claude Opus 4.6, Claude Sonnet 5, and Claude Sonnet 4.6 advisors return a 400 error. The advice comes back encrypted as an `advisor_redacted_result` block, so its text isn't readable in the response."}]}
{"id":"c19","kind":"web","text":"tool call 사이 한두 문장보다 긴 메모는 progress-update thinking 블록으로 오고 기본 display 에서 비어 있다 (08장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d1 §Text between tool calls","evidence":[{"source":"d1","locator":"§Text between tool calls ¶1","quote":"On Claude Sonnet 5.5, notes longer than a sentence or two that the model writes between tool calls come back as [progress-update `thinking` blocks](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/thinking#progress-updates), empty at the default `display`. Shorter remarks stay `text`."}]}
{"id":"c20","kind":"web","text":"adaptive 에서 display updates 는 beta 이고 header thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18 이 필요하다 (08, 14장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d1 §Text between tool calls","evidence":[{"source":"d1","locator":"§Text between tool calls ¶2","quote":"With adaptive thinking, set `display` to `\"updates\"` (beta, `thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18` header) to get the updates alone, or to `\"summarized\"` to get them mixed with reasoning. Render each non-empty `thinking` block before the `tool_use` block that follows it. With [`between_tools`](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/models/sonnet-5-5/migration-guide#turn-off-up-front-thinking), the text comes back without `display`."}]}
{"id":"c21","kind":"web","text":"display 와 무관하게 과금은 같고 reasoning 토큰은 usage.output_tokens_details.thinking_tokens 로 확인한다 (08장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d2 §Pricing","evidence":[{"source":"d2","locator":"§Pricing","quote":"What you're billed for is the same regardless of the `display` setting; only what you see changes:"},{"source":"d2","locator":"§Pricing ¶3","quote":"To see how many billed output tokens were spent on internal reasoning, read `usage.output_tokens_details.thinking_tokens` in the response."}]}
{"id":"c22","kind":"web","text":"thinking 은 max_tokens 안에 들어가고 출력 토큰으로 과금되며 stop_reason max_tokens 에는 두 처방이 있다 (08, 14장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d1 §Handle thinking, d2 §Cost control","evidence":[{"source":"d1","locator":"§Handle thinking in responses","quote":"* **Revisit `max_tokens`.** It covers thinking plus text, and thinking tokens are billed as output tokens."},{"source":"d2","locator":"§Cost control","quote":"If you see [`stop_reason: \"max_tokens\"`](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/thinking-troubleshooting#stopped-at-max-tokens) in responses, you have two remedies:"}]}
{"id":"c23","kind":"web","text":"Sonnet 5.5 는 Sonnet 5 보다 많은 부류에서 거부하고 stop_details 부류는 cyber, bio, frontier_llm, reasoning_extraction, general_harms 다 (02, 09장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d1 §Safety classifiers and fallback","evidence":[{"source":"d1","locator":"§Safety classifiers and fallback","quote":"Claude Sonnet 5.5 declines in more categories than Claude Sonnet 5. A decline returns `stop_reason: \"refusal\"`, and its `stop_details` can name one of these [categories](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/refusals-and-fallback#refusal-response):"},{"source":"d1","locator":"§Safety classifiers and fallback","quote":"* **`\"general_harms\"`:** The request falls under another usage-policy area. Benign work can also trigger this category."}]}
{"id":"c24","kind":"web","text":"server-side fallback 은 beta, Claude API 전용이고 cyber 와 frontier_llm 만 Sonnet 5 로 재시도한다 (02, 09, 14, 18장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d1 §Safety classifiers and fallback","evidence":[{"source":"d1","locator":"§Safety classifiers and fallback ¶2","quote":"[Server-side fallback](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/refusals-and-fallback#server-side-fallback) (`fallbacks: \"default\"`, beta, Claude API only) retries `\"cyber\"` and `\"frontier_llm\"` declines on Claude Sonnet 5. It doesn't retry `\"bio\"`, `\"reasoning_extraction\"`, or `\"general_harms\"` declines."}]}
{"id":"c25","kind":"web","text":"높은 위험의 cyber 작업은 Sonnet 5 로 눈에 보이게 넘어가고 일상적 버그 수정은 막히지 않는다 (09장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w1 §Safety · Cybersecurity","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Safety · Safeguards · Cybersecurity","quote":"Users can still find and fix bugs in their code as part of routine software development, but higher-risk cybersecurity tasks will visibly fall back to Sonnet 5."}]}
{"id":"c26","kind":"web","text":"bio 분류기는 미생물학과 바이러스학 요청 일부를 잘못 걸 수 있다 (09, 17장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w1 §Safety · Biology","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Safety · Safeguards · Biology","quote":"These target harmful requests; most research, education, and clinical work is unaffected, though some microbiology and virology requests may be flagged in error."}]}
{"id":"c27","kind":"web","text":"Sonnet 4.6 이하에서 옮기는 코드에는 실시간 cyber 안전장치가 처음이다 (09장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d1 §Safety classifiers and fallback","evidence":[{"source":"d1","locator":"§Safety classifiers and fallback ¶3","quote":"Real-time cyber safeguards are new for code from Claude Sonnet 4.6, Claude Sonnet 4.5, and Claude Haiku 4.5. For legitimate security work, apply to the [Cyber Verification Program](https://support.claude.com/en/articles/14604842-real-time-cyber-safeguards-on-claude-opus-and-sonnet)."}]}
{"id":"c28","kind":"web","text":"Sonnet 5.5 는 cyber 능력이 Opus 5 에 견줄 만해 Sonnet 최초로 cyber 안전장치와 fallback 을 달았고 bio 는 Sonnet 5 와 같다 (03장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w1 §intro · Alignment and safety","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§intro · Alignment and safety","quote":"Because its cybersecurity capabilities are comparable to Opus 5’s, it’s the first Sonnet model to launch with cyber safeguards and fallbacks like those we’ve developed for our most capable models. Its biology safeguards are the same as Sonnet 5’s."}]}
{"id":"c29","kind":"web","text":"캐시 최소 프롬프트가 1,024 에서 512 토큰으로 내려갔다 (10장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d1 §Other changes","evidence":[{"source":"d1","locator":"§Other changes","quote":"* **Prompt caching:** The minimum cacheable prompt is 512 tokens, down from 1,024 on Claude Sonnet 5, Claude Sonnet 4.6, and Claude Sonnet 4.5."}]}
{"id":"c30","kind":"web","text":"effort 를 바꾸면 캐시 breakpoint 가 무효가 되고 기본값을 명시하는 것은 캐시를 깨지 않는다 (10, 14장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d2 §Prompt caching","evidence":[{"source":"d2","locator":"§Prompt caching","quote":"The resolved effort value is rendered into the prompt, so changing it between requests invalidates cache breakpoints, just as changing the legacy [`budget_tokens`](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/extended-thinking#extended-thinking-with-prompt-caching) parameter does on models that use it. Setting `effort` explicitly to the model's default is equivalent to omitting it and does not break the cache."}]}
{"id":"c31","kind":"numeric","text":"가격표: Sonnet 5.5 캐시 읽기 $0.20, 캐시 쓰기 $2.50, 입력 $2, 출력 $10, Opus 5.5 는 $0.20, $5, $4, $20 (10장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w1 §Cost and speed · pricing table","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Cost and speed · pricing table","quote":"Cache reads$0.20$0.20Cache writes$2.50$5Input tokens$2$4Output tokens$10$20"}]}
{"id":"c32","kind":"web","text":"Claude API 기본 effort 는 high 이고 단계가 다시 조정되어 같은 이름이 Sonnet 5 와 같은 thinking 양을 내지 않는다 (02, 11, 17장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d1 §Recommended changes","evidence":[{"source":"d1","locator":"§Recommended changes","quote":"Re-run your effort sweep. Claude Sonnet 5.5 has five effort levels: `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`, and `max`. The default on the Claude API is `high`. The levels are recalibrated, so a level doesn't produce the same amount of thinking as on Claude Sonnet 5."}]}
{"id":"c33","kind":"web","text":"Claude Code 와 앱의 기본 effort 는 Medium, Claude Platform 은 High 다 (11장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w1 §Cost and speed ¶2","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Cost and speed ¶2","quote":"In Claude Code and our apps, the default effort is set to Medium, while the Claude Platform defaults to High."}]}
{"id":"c34","kind":"web","text":"thinking 문서는 high 를 대부분 모델의 기본, medium 을 Opus 5.5 의 기본으로 적는다 (11장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d2 §Effort levels","evidence":[{"source":"d2","locator":"§Effort levels · table","quote":"| `high` (default on most models)       | Claude thinks on most requests that benefit from it. Provides deep reasoning on complex tasks.   |"},{"source":"d2","locator":"§Effort levels · table","quote":"| `medium` (default on Claude Opus 5.5) | Claude uses moderate thinking. May skip thinking for simple queries.                             |"}]}
{"id":"c35","kind":"web","text":"guide 는 일반은 high, agentic 코딩은 medium 에서 high, 지연에 민감한 일은 medium 이나 low 에서 시작하라고 권한다 (11장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d1 §Recommended changes","evidence":[{"source":"d1","locator":"§Recommended changes","quote":"Start at `high` unless your workload is agentic or latency-sensitive. For agentic coding and multistep tool use, start at `medium` for well-specified tasks and move to `high` for harder or longer ones. For chat and other latency-sensitive work, start at `medium` or `low`."}]}
{"id":"c36","kind":"web","text":"guide 체크리스트의 마지막 항목은 effort sweep 을 다시 돌리고 비용 기준선을 새로 잡는 것이다 (14장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"d1 §Migration checklist","evidence":[{"source":"d1","locator":"§Migration checklist · Every starting model","quote":"* [Re-run your effort sweep](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/models/sonnet-5-5/migration-guide#recommended-changes), and re-baseline cost."}]}
